From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:11:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 46/47] core: draft head rope, sigmoid gate and add kernels

Three BF16 draft primitives for a gated attention block: an in-place NeoX rope
over the first `rotary` dims of each head (partial rope), Y = X * sigmoid(gate)
with each head's gate the second half of its [query, gate] pair in the q
projection, and a row add. `zig build test-draft-ops` checks them on 16 heads
of 256 at positions 0, 63 and 2048: the gate and the add bit-exact against
their formulas, the rope within one BF16 step and dims past `rotary` untouched.
---
